# The author's example (2026-10-05; HEAD-ROLE-UNESTABLISHED-ROWS). f has no
# formal x, no x in its sight and no read of x before `x: j`, so `x: j`
# defines a named Structure x, and returning it from a method whose result
# is int is a type error. g's own x does not change the role of f's head,
# and the later `return: x` does not make x an input after the fact.
fn: f () int
    int: j 3
    x: j
    return: x
end: f

fn: g () int
    int: x 4
    return: f()
end: g

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: g(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
